# If you cite this work, this is the canonical machine-readable form.
# Renders on the GitHub repository page as a "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Cabinet of Shadows: A Victorian alienist's casebook of the monsters of Gothic literature"
message: "If you reference this work in academic or editorial writing, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Caules
    given-names: Frank
    email: frank.caules@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/frankcaules/cabinet-of-shadows"
url: "https://cabinetofshadows.me"
abstract: >
  An interactive, long-form science-communication site presenting thirteen
  classic monsters of nineteenth-century Gothic literature as the patients
  of an unnamed Victorian alienist. Each dossier pairs a literary reading
  of the source novel with a contemporary peer-reviewed psychological
  phenomenon — including disorganised attachment, clinical lycanthropy,
  mass sociogenic illness, depersonalisation, the Unheimliche, and
  narcissistic personality structure — with full, live-DOI citations.
  Bilingual in English and Thai.
keywords:
  - gothic literature
  - psychology of horror
  - science communication
  - clinical lycanthropy
  - disorganised attachment
  - depersonalisation
  - mass sociogenic illness
  - the Unheimliche
  - Dracula
  - Frankenstein
  - Mr Hyde
  - bilingual
  - Thai
